                "of": {
                  "op": "mem_bits",
                  "at": {
                    "addr": "0x2001E030"
                  },
                  "width": 4,
                  "mask": 1,
                  "cmp": "eq",
                  "value": 1
                }
              },
              {
                "op": "not",
                "of": {
                  "op": "mem_bits",
                  "at": {
                    "addr": "0x2001E040"
                  },
                  "width": 4,
                  "mask": 1,
                  "cmp": "eq",
                  "value": 1
                }
              },
              {
                "op": "not",
                "of": {
                  "op": "mem_bits",
                  "at": {
                    "addr": "0x2001E050"
                  },
                  "width": 4,
                  "mask": 1,
                  "cmp": "eq",
                  "value": 1
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "Fewer reporting instruments means less recorder fill, but the brief is to keep telemetry intact. Restore the instruments and fix the recorder instead."
        },
        {
          "when": {
            "op": "all",
            "of": [
              {
                "op": "mem_changed",
                "at": {
                  "sym": "task_recorder"
                },
                "len": 124
              },
              {
                "op": "tlm",
                "path": "channels.HK.rec_fill_pct",
                "cmp": "gt",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "text": "The recorder code has changed, but the buffer is not empty. A patch that stops the task leaves the backlog where it was; a patch that lets it drain needs time. Which did you write?"
        }
      ],
      "hints": [
        {
          "after_frames": 6,
          "text": "Housekeeping reports the recorder's fill level. The recorder is a scheduled function with an eight-byte entry pad and a second patch point in its body."
        },
        {
          "after_frames": 18,
          "text": "A return from a function can be encoded in Thumb without rewriting its whole body. So can zeroing the register that holds what it generates."
        }
      ]
    },
